# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=production

# ── Authentication: Authentik (OIDC) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Login is delegated to a self-hosted Authentik instance (stood up by the
# home-lab-utils repo: `./authentik.sh up`). Create an OAuth2/OpenID provider +
# application (slug `myfinancehub`) in Authentik, then set these. On the homelab
# box, put OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET (and the rest) in the host-only finance.env file
# that deploy.sh injects with --env-file — never commit the secret.
#
# Use the homelab HOST IP (not a container DNS name) for the issuer so the OIDC
# `iss` claim matches what the browser and the app server both reach.
# OIDC_ISSUER=http://<homelab-ip>:9000/application/o/myfinancehub/
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# ── Roles (Authentik groups → app role) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Three roles: admin > member > viewer (admin = everything, member = everyday
# writes, viewer = read-only). The role is taken from the user's Authentik group,
# delivered in the OIDC `groups` claim, and re-evaluated on every login.
# Authentik's DEFAULT `profile` scope mapping already emits `groups`, so no custom
# scope mapping is needed — just create the three groups and assign users.
# WARNING: once groups flow, a user in NONE of the groups becomes `viewer` on next
# login — add your admin user to finance-admins BEFORE enabling, or lose access.
# OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email          # default; groups arrives via `profile`
# OIDC_ADMIN_GROUP=finance-admins
# OIDC_MEMBER_GROUP=finance-members
# OIDC_VIEWER_GROUP=finance-viewers
# OIDC_DEFAULT_ROLE=viewer                 # role when a user is in none of the groups
#
# OIDC_PUBLIC_BASE — set this only when Authentik is also exposed over Tailscale so
# login works OFF-LAN. It is the public Authentik ORIGIN (scheme+host[:port]) that
# the BROWSER can reach. For https (Tailscale) requests the app rewrites just the
# authorize URL's origin to this; discovery/token/jwks still use the LAN OIDC_ISSUER
# (which the container reaches directly), so the `iss` claim keeps validating.
#   tailscale serve --bg --https=8443 http://localhost:9200   # on the homelab
# OIDC_PUBLIC_BASE=https://<machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net:8443
#
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI is now only a FALLBACK. The app derives the callback from the
# origin each request arrives on (honouring Tailscale's X-Forwarded-* headers), so
# it works on both the LAN URL and the Tailscale HTTPS URL without bouncing you to
# a single host. IMPORTANT: register EVERY origin's `/auth/callback` on the
# Authentik provider — easiest is a Redirect URIs *regex* covering both, e.g.
#   ^http://<homelab-ip>:3090/.*$
#   ^https://<machine>\.<tailnet>\.ts\.net/.*$
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://<homelab-ip>:3090/auth/callback
# Set to ANY value to enable RP-initiated logout (clears the Authentik SSO session
# too). The post-logout target is derived from the request origin, not this value.
# OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=1

# ── Session Secret (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If not set, one is auto-generated and stored in the database.
# Only set this if you need sessions to survive a full database reset.
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Monthly report email via Resend ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for the month-end report email. NEVER commit the real key.
# On the homelab box, put these in the host-only file /home/phanikumar/finance-hub/finance.env
# (chmod 600) — deploy.sh injects it into the container with --env-file.
# Get a key at https://resend.com/api-keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# REPORT_EMAIL_FROM=onboarding@resend.dev
# REPORT_EMAIL_TO=maruthi.phanikumar@yahoo.com
# Optional: also mirror the report to Slack as a Block Kit card. Best-effort —
# a bad/missing webhook is logged and ignored, the email still sends. Host-managed
# in finance.env like the keys above. Create one at
# https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks (Incoming Webhooks). Unset = email-only.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/xxx/yyy/zzz

# Optional: bearer token that gates GET /api/digest — the read-only weekly finance
# AGGREGATES (totals/deltas/top categories, never raw transactions) the homelab's
# Sunday digest workflow fetches over the LAN. Set the SAME value as the homelab's
# FINANCE_DIGEST_TOKEN. Host-managed in finance.env. Unset = endpoint disabled (503).
# DIGEST_TOKEN=a-long-random-shared-secret

# ── Local LLM: oMLX (shared by "Ask" + receipt extraction) ────────────────────
# Inference runs on the homelab Mac mini via oMLX (https://github.com/jundot/omlx),
# which REPLACED Ollama (2026-07-29). oMLX is OpenAI-compatible, NOT
# Ollama-compatible: it serves POST /v1/chat/completions and does NOT serve
# /api/generate, so the base URL must end in /v1 and the port is 8000 (not 11434).
#
# Three things must be true on the Mac mini or nothing off-box can use it:
#  1. `server.host` in ~/.omlx/settings.json is "0.0.0.0" — oMLX binds 127.0.0.1
#     by DEFAULT, so a fresh install is unreachable from the container. (This
#     replaces the old OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 requirement.)
#  2. The model is downloaded through the oMLX admin panel (it lands in
#     ~/.omlx/models) — there is no `ollama pull`. The real installed model id is
#     `mlx-community/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-4bit`, served as `gemma-3-4b-it-qat-4bit`.
#  3. An ALIAS named `gemma3:4b` points at that model in the oMLX admin panel.
#     Every *_MODEL value below is that alias, so if the alias is missing the
#     calls fail with an unknown-model error — recreate the alias, or set the
#     *_MODEL vars to the real id above.
# Use the homelab HOST IP (not localhost / host.docker.internal) so the container
# can reach it. Both features degrade gracefully when oMLX is unreachable.

# LLM_BASE_URL — app-wide oMLX base URL, used by receipt extraction and (unless
# overridden below) by "Ask". Must end in /v1.
LLM_BASE_URL=http://192.168.50.141:8000/v1
# LLM_API_KEY — REQUIRED. oMLX authenticates every request (Ollama had no auth at
# all); it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. SECRET — never commit the real
# value. Host-managed in finance.env / a GitHub repo Secret that deploy.yml syncs.
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL — model (alias) used for receipt extraction; must be vision-capable.
# GitHub-managed (repo Variable LLM_MODEL); deploy.yml syncs it into finance.env.
LLM_MODEL=gemma3:4b
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS — abort a receipt-extraction call after this many ms. Receipt
# images are big and vision decoding is slow, hence the generous default 120000.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# ── Natural-language query ("Ask") ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The "Ask" view turns a plain-English question into a READ-ONLY SQL SELECT using
# the local oMLX model — your finance data never leaves the homelab. It shares
# LLM_API_KEY with receipt extraction and inherits LLM_BASE_URL; the vars below
# only exist so "Ask" can be pointed at a different box/model/timeout (e.g. a
# smaller, faster text-only model) without touching the receipt pipeline.
# NLQUERY_LLM_BASE_URL — optional override; unset = use LLM_BASE_URL.
# NLQUERY_LLM_BASE_URL=http://192.168.50.141:8000/v1
# NLQUERY_LLM_MODEL — model for NL→SQL translation + summarising (default gemma3:4b).
# NLQUERY_LLM_MODEL=gemma3:4b
# NLQUERY_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS — abort the model call after this many ms. Much lower
# than the receipt timeout because a user is waiting on the response (default 30000).
# NLQUERY_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# NLQUERY_ENABLED — set to 0/false/off to disable the Ask feature entirely.
# NLQUERY_ENABLED=1

# ── DEPRECATED Ollama-era vars (still honored, do not set for new installs) ───
# The code keeps reading these as fallbacks ONLY so a half-finished migration (new
# image, host finance.env not yet updated) keeps working. They carry Ollama's port
# 11434 and /api/generate path, which oMLX does not serve — the client logs a
# warning and normalizes what it can. Delete them once the new vars are set.
#   OLLAMA_BASE_URL   → superseded by NLQUERY_LLM_BASE_URL / LLM_BASE_URL
#   OLLAMA_MODEL      → superseded by NLQUERY_LLM_MODEL
#   OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS → superseded by NLQUERY_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS
#   LLM_URL           → superseded by LLM_BASE_URL (was a full /api/generate URL)
